From: DE25-Nano port
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reassert sixteen-row OSD for every full menu

Older OSD implementations clear their high-resolution latch on each disable
transaction. Main can later enable a partially updated screen without writing
line 8, leaving only the upper eight rows visible. Reassert the geometry from
Main's requested row count immediately before every enable transaction.

diff --git a/osd.cpp b/osd.cpp
--- a/osd.cpp
+++ b/osd.cpp
@@ -502,6 +502,11 @@ void OsdEnable(unsigned char mode)
 {
 	user_io_osd_key_enable(mode & DISABLE_KEYBOARD);
 	mode &= (DISABLE_KEYBOARD | OSD_MSG);
+	// Reassert high-resolution geometry whenever the active UI owns more than
+	// eight rows. The FPGA clears its height latch on disable, and an in-core
+	// menu may be enabled before its lower rows are redrawn. Derive the command
+	// from Main's requested size rather than from the loaded core persona.
+	if (osd_size > 8) spi_osd_cmd(OSD_CMD_WRITE | 8);
 	spi_osd_cmd(OSD_CMD_ENABLE | mode);
 }
 
